      "explanation": "The real logarithms require \\(m>0\\) and \\(n>0\\). Add \\(\\log_{10}n\\) to both sides so that the product rule can combine the two logarithms:\n\\[\n\\log_{10}(mn)=\\log_{10}m+\\log_{10}n=b.\n\\]\nBy the definition of a base-10 logarithm, this means \\(mn=10^b\\). Because \\(n>0\\), division by \\(n\\) is valid, giving\n\\[\nm=\\frac{10^b}{n}.\n\\]\nThis is choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
      "id": "combine-logarithms",
